import EulersGem.ExplicitRegular

/-!
# The regular icosahedron

Vertices: the twelve points `(0, ±1, ±φ)` and their cyclic permutations (`φ = Real.goldenRatio`). The face lattice, counts, face type and
flag-transitivity are all decided by the kernel (`decide +kernel`, no `native_decide`) from
the certificate data below, generated by `lean/scripts/platonic_gen.py` and
`lean/scripts/platonic_emit_lean.py`.

* `icosaData.pts` — the 12 vertices in `ℤ[φ]³`;
* `icosaData.facets` / `.edges` — the 20 facets and 30 edges as vertex-index lists;
* `icosaData.certs` — for each of the 36 non-adjacent vertex pairs, nonnegative weights
  showing the midpoint is a convex combination of the other vertices;
* `icosaSym` — three mirror normals, the vertex permutations they induce, and a word for each of
  the 120 flags.
-/

namespace EulersGem

namespace Platonic3

open Explicit ZPhi

